  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 107 AM CDT Thu Apr 16 2026\n\nThe next strong storm system with a sharper dryline will move into \nthe Central and Southern Plains Friday. Looks like the more \norganized severe weather will remain north of our area. However, \nisolated severe thunderstorms are possible across west central \nTexas during the late afternoon into Friday night. A cold front is\nsouth of the area by Saturday morning with cooler and mainly dry \nweather this weekend into early next week. However, return \nsoutherly flow may result in a low chance of showers and a few \nthunderstorms early next week. Temperatures will be slightly above\nnormal this week. Please keep up with the latest weather \ninformation as the month of April is severe weather season.",
